WEBVTT

00:00:02.900 --> 00:00:04.370
<i>Capeta...{ep41 17:21}</i>

00:00:04.370 --> 00:00:08.030
<i>You were always being held back because of an old kart and I couldn't see it until now.</i>

00:00:08.660 --> 00:00:12.870
<i>So this is how you've been driving, all this time.</i>

00:00:14.700 --> 00:00:18.100
<i>I asked him like that, but...</i>

00:00:19.870 --> 00:00:23.760
<i>Honestly, the one who wanted to continue racing as Team Capeta...</i>

00:00:25.120 --> 00:00:27.570
<i>was... me.</i>

00:00:31.770 --> 00:00:32.510
<i>Okay!</i>

00:00:32.510 --> 00:00:34.270
<i>I'll have this lap!</i>

00:00:34.270 --> 00:00:36.770
<i>If I'm to beat Shiba, this is the lap!</i>

00:00:37.220 --> 00:00:39.730
<i>I'm going to be the one getting the scholarship!</i>

00:00:42.280 --> 00:00:45.240
<i>Isa spins on the fifth corner!</i>

00:00:45.710 --> 00:00:46.240
<i>Oh no!</i>

00:00:46.240 --> 00:00:48.570
<i>Taira, look out!  Dodge it!</i>

00:00:52.370 --> 00:00:53.870
<i>Don't hit!</i>

00:00:54.710 --> 00:00:56.770
<i>Taira, dodge it!</i>

00:01:07.840 --> 00:01:09.560
<i>What was that noise?</i>

00:01:09.560 --> 00:01:11.970
<i>Huh, what?  What happened?</i>

00:01:11.970 --> 00:01:13.810
<i>I... don't know, but...</i>

00:01:13.810 --> 00:01:16.140
<i>Is that... Capeta?</i>

00:01:16.140 --> 00:01:18.710
Hey!  Are you all right?!

00:01:23.420 --> 00:01:24.660
Can you talk?

00:01:24.660 --> 00:01:26.650
Are you hurt anywhere?

00:01:26.650 --> 00:01:28.380
I'm going to take the belt off.

00:01:28.380 --> 00:01:29.790
Can you stand?

00:01:29.790 --> 00:01:31.360
Y-Yes.

00:01:50.760 --> 00:01:53.450
<i>What... is this?</i>

00:01:54.220 --> 00:01:55.970
Yes, both of them.

00:01:55.970 --> 00:01:57.600
Yeah, they're safe.

00:01:57.600 --> 00:01:59.630
No injuries.  Right.

00:01:59.630 --> 00:02:03.380
Taira, Isa, get out over the fence with your helmets on.

00:02:03.380 --> 00:02:04.690
Hurry!

00:02:05.360 --> 00:02:06.990
<i>Why did this happen?!</i>

00:02:07.600 --> 00:02:09.940
<i>Everything was going so well!</i>

00:02:13.620 --> 00:02:15.340
T-Taira...

00:02:16.450 --> 00:02:17.330
I'm sorry.

00:02:21.480 --> 00:02:22.250
Sorry.

00:02:22.250 --> 00:02:23.490
It couldn't be helped.

00:02:24.040 --> 00:02:26.130
It's not your fault.

00:02:26.130 --> 00:02:28.880
So both Taira and Isa are unhurt.

00:02:30.120 --> 00:02:31.050
Thank goodness.

00:02:31.470 --> 00:02:32.290
Okay.

00:02:32.290 --> 00:02:36.000
Pick up any small fragments you can.

00:02:36.340 --> 00:02:37.750
<b>Session finished!</b>

00:02:37.750 --> 00:02:40.480
<b>All cars pit in slowly.</b>

00:02:42.520 --> 00:02:44.630
It's the rear suspension.

00:02:44.630 --> 00:02:46.580
How about the other car?

00:02:48.360 --> 00:02:50.280
So he's done it...

00:02:57.280 --> 00:02:58.720
H-Hey...

00:02:59.860 --> 00:03:02.540
How much... do you think it's going to be?

00:03:14.800 --> 00:03:16.850
<i>Now listen, Capeta.</i>

00:03:16.850 --> 00:03:19.190
<i>Whatever you do, be careful not to crash.</i>

00:03:19.190 --> 00:03:20.810
<i>It's not just about the money.</i>

00:03:21.320 --> 00:03:25.730
<i>They say that if you crash a FSte machine, there's no chance for you to pass.</i>

00:03:26.350 --> 00:03:30.280
<i>So let's be more cautious than when we were in karts.</i>

00:03:30.770 --> 00:03:32.780
<i>All right, Capeta?</i>

00:03:35.760 --> 00:03:39.300
<i>You go fight in my place.</i>

00:03:39.300 --> 00:03:42.420
<i>I'm saying I'll give you the money for the audition.</i>

00:03:47.210 --> 00:03:50.050
<i>Say that again once you've seen this! {ep34 04:30 - not an exact match}</i>

00:03:59.250 --> 00:04:00.800
<i>It's over...</i>

00:05:45.950 --> 00:05:47.710
U-Umm...

00:05:47.710 --> 00:05:51.060
I'm Taira Capeta's father.

00:05:55.660 --> 00:05:58.930
Is it over for my son?

00:05:58.930 --> 00:06:00.640
Is he disqualified?

00:06:00.640 --> 00:06:01.920
No.

00:06:01.920 --> 00:06:03.750
That's not the case.

00:06:04.290 --> 00:06:05.650
But...

00:06:07.980 --> 00:06:12.470
The cost of repairs from that crash will be calculated from the actual expenses of the parts.

00:06:12.470 --> 00:06:15.320
We will quickly calculate it and send you a bill.

00:06:18.540 --> 00:06:23.130
But students are nervous after a crash.

00:06:23.130 --> 00:06:25.830
They're scared of crashing again.

00:06:26.250 --> 00:06:31.290
It's up to the student and their parents whether to continue or not.

00:06:33.060 --> 00:06:36.510
E-Even if he continues,
 is it impossible for him to pass?

00:06:38.010 --> 00:06:39.890
It's not impossible, but...

00:06:40.750 --> 00:06:42.720
he's certainly at a disadvantage.

00:07:10.520 --> 00:07:11.420
Capeta!

00:07:14.970 --> 00:07:17.210
Are you sure you're not hurt?

00:07:21.880 --> 00:07:23.830
Cheer up!

00:07:23.830 --> 00:07:25.560
You still have a chance!

00:07:25.560 --> 00:07:26.100
Okay?

00:07:27.150 --> 00:07:28.560
<i>A chance?</i>

00:07:34.220 --> 00:07:35.420
Father.

00:07:36.210 --> 00:07:37.850
If you'll please.

00:07:37.850 --> 00:07:39.070
Y-Yes.

00:07:44.180 --> 00:07:46.200
It's about the charge for the repairs...

00:07:46.200 --> 00:07:52.000
I can't give you an exact price, but it'll be around 1.5 to 2 million yen.

00:07:52.000 --> 00:07:54.460
Two... Two million yen?!

00:08:54.890 --> 00:08:57.190
Stand up, Capeta.

00:08:58.900 --> 00:09:00.900
You can do the final, right?

00:09:03.470 --> 00:09:04.360
But...

00:09:04.360 --> 00:09:08.630
I'll do something about the charge for the repairs.

00:09:08.630 --> 00:09:09.830
Don't worry about it.

00:09:10.560 --> 00:09:11.700
You'll do something about it?!

00:09:11.700 --> 00:09:13.540
But how?!

00:09:13.540 --> 00:09:15.330
I heard something like 2 million yen!

00:09:15.330 --> 00:09:21.340
I-If a big adult puts his mind to it, 2 or 3 million yen is nothing!

00:09:21.340 --> 00:09:23.340
<i>U-Uncle...</i>

00:09:23.340 --> 00:09:25.480
<i>Just don't do anything dangerous.</i>

00:09:26.470 --> 00:09:28.260
<i>Could it be that?</i>

00:09:30.720 --> 00:09:34.250
Capeta, don't worry about the money anymore.

00:09:34.250 --> 00:09:36.190
Concentrate on the race.

00:09:36.520 --> 00:09:37.870
But...

00:09:37.870 --> 00:09:40.980
they said I'll never pass if I break a machine.

00:09:41.550 --> 00:09:44.370
There's no point in doing it anymore!

00:09:46.810 --> 00:09:48.280
Capeta, calm down.

00:09:49.740 --> 00:09:52.590
Is racing just a hobby?

00:09:52.590 --> 00:09:54.920
Or do you want to be a racer?

00:09:55.460 --> 00:09:57.250
I... I never...

00:09:57.250 --> 00:09:59.710
If you never thought about it, decide now.

00:10:00.120 --> 00:10:04.170
When I saw you out there today, I thought you should be a racer.

00:10:04.730 --> 00:10:08.750
You should also be thinking you want to be a racer.

00:10:08.750 --> 00:10:10.670
That's why I'll give you the money.

00:10:10.670 --> 00:10:13.730
Your chances may be slim, but it's not like they're gone completely.

00:10:13.730 --> 00:10:15.850
Don't give up on them until the very end.

00:10:16.330 --> 00:10:17.850
Dad...

00:10:19.380 --> 00:10:23.320
However, this is as far as I can help you.

00:10:24.480 --> 00:10:25.820
I'm at my limit.

00:10:27.180 --> 00:10:30.780
From here on, you open your own future.

00:10:32.280 --> 00:10:35.170
<i>I'm sorry that I'm an unreliable dad.</i>

00:10:35.170 --> 00:10:40.790
<i>But from here on, I can't go with you.</i>

00:10:42.240 --> 00:10:45.210
I'll take on everything up to today!

00:10:45.210 --> 00:10:48.110
So go until your heart's content!

00:10:50.530 --> 00:10:52.350
Okay, Capeta?

00:10:52.780 --> 00:10:56.310
Ca-chan, there's no point if you give up now!

00:10:58.270 --> 00:10:59.580
Monami...

00:11:12.070 --> 00:11:13.850
Umm, excuse me!

00:11:13.850 --> 00:11:16.580
He'll be participating in the finals so please look after him!

00:11:16.580 --> 00:11:18.030
Okay.

00:11:18.030 --> 00:11:19.540
I understand.

00:11:36.630 --> 00:11:39.350
<b>Last of the qualifiers!  Ten minutes remaining!</b>

00:11:39.350 --> 00:11:40.620
<b>Everyone...</b>

00:11:40.620 --> 00:11:41.940
do your best!

00:11:43.930 --> 00:11:48.640
We're preparing the spare machine now,
 but it won't be ready before the qualifier finishes.

00:11:48.640 --> 00:11:53.410
So the time you got before the crash, 31.18 seconds, will be your qualifying time.

00:11:53.410 --> 00:11:53.910
Okay?

00:11:53.910 --> 00:11:55.120
Yes.

00:11:56.310 --> 00:11:57.580
About that crash...

00:11:59.370 --> 00:12:01.570
You can't see ahead on that fifth corner,

00:12:01.570 --> 00:12:05.590
and if you have a car spinning in front of you right at the moment you're attacking,

00:12:05.590 --> 00:12:08.000
I think crashing is unavoidable.

00:12:09.170 --> 00:12:10.510
Listen.

00:12:10.510 --> 00:12:14.930
Crashing is part of the race too, so don't let that scare you and slow you down.

00:12:15.480 --> 00:12:18.890
Go into that corner the next time as before.

00:12:22.640 --> 00:12:24.900
That was very good.

00:12:32.280 --> 00:12:33.590
Taira.

00:12:33.590 --> 00:12:34.520
We'll adjust the pedals.

00:12:34.520 --> 00:12:35.530
Hurry up.

00:12:35.530 --> 00:12:36.240
Yes!

00:12:37.470 --> 00:12:38.660
<i>That's right.</i>

00:12:39.790 --> 00:12:41.400
<i>That's right!</i>

00:12:42.910 --> 00:12:45.880
<i>No one said you're disqualified!</i>

00:12:46.370 --> 00:12:48.680
<i>It's not like I've failed!</i>

00:12:50.080 --> 00:12:51.510
<i>The final...</i>

00:12:51.910 --> 00:12:53.130
<i>I'll do it.</i>

00:13:04.730 --> 00:13:08.270
<b>Good, it's Hata!  She's also shortened her time!</b>

00:13:08.270 --> 00:13:09.980
<b>31.16 seconds!</b>

00:13:10.380 --> 00:13:15.990
She's 0.02 seconds faster than Taira's record before the crash!

00:13:15.990 --> 00:13:17.180
What?!

00:13:17.180 --> 00:13:19.450
31.16 seconds?

00:13:19.980 --> 00:13:21.250
She got us.

00:13:21.250 --> 00:13:25.010
I thought we could keep the 3rd grid.

00:13:25.010 --> 00:13:27.670
It doesn't matter which grid he's on.

00:13:30.230 --> 00:13:32.120
<b>Session finished!</b>

00:13:38.050 --> 00:13:39.210
I beat Taira?!

00:13:39.210 --> 00:13:40.590
Is that true?

00:13:40.590 --> 00:13:42.880
Yeah, 31.16 seconds.

00:13:42.880 --> 00:13:44.780
You're in 3rd place.

00:13:44.780 --> 00:13:46.100
All right!

00:13:49.520 --> 00:13:54.500
<i>Just because you were a little faster, you got in over your head and ended up in a crash.</i>

00:13:54.500 --> 00:13:58.750
<i>When they say not to break the machine, you should never break it.</i>

00:14:00.040 --> 00:14:04.700
<i>You don't have the right to be a professional when you can't do as you're told.</i>

00:14:05.290 --> 00:14:08.420
<i>You just go and play along with those friends of yours.</i>

00:14:08.820 --> 00:14:11.490
<i>The ones who win are those who race seriously.</i>

00:14:11.490 --> 00:14:13.380
<i>God is always watching!</i>

00:14:15.860 --> 00:14:18.840
Hey.  Are you all right?

00:14:19.280 --> 00:14:20.730
That was bad luck.

00:14:21.330 --> 00:14:22.900
But you can race in the finals, right?

00:14:22.900 --> 00:14:23.810
That's good.

00:14:23.800 --> 00:14:25.310
Y-Yeah.

00:14:32.130 --> 00:14:35.150
Well, I'll win again in the final, though.

00:14:36.030 --> 00:14:37.670
Haruna and today...

00:14:37.670 --> 00:14:40.070
If I win continuously, it means I'm the real thing.{it's talent.}

00:15:33.330 --> 00:15:35.020
<i>It's no good.</i>

00:15:35.020 --> 00:15:37.970
<i>It doesn't look like he'll be able to overtake him.</i>

00:15:37.970 --> 00:15:40.610
<i>My head is still messed up, too.</i>

00:15:40.610 --> 00:15:43.740
<i>That crushed machine is burned into my eyes.</i>

00:15:44.330 --> 00:15:47.430
<i>Moreover, it's him who crashed it.</i>

00:15:47.920 --> 00:15:50.850
<i>I've never seen Capeta like this.</i>

00:15:53.440 --> 00:15:55.900
<b>It's finally here!</b>

00:15:55.900 --> 00:15:58.380
<b>FSRS mock race final!</b>

00:15:58.380 --> 00:16:01.860
<b>In the grandstand there's 35,000... eh?</b>

00:16:01.860 --> 00:16:03.860
Enough?

00:16:03.860 --> 00:16:05.910
<b>Pole position is Ishihara.</b>

00:16:05.910 --> 00:16:10.870
<b>Showing his pride as FSRS's driver; his last record was 30.64 seconds!</b>

00:16:10.870 --> 00:16:14.080
<b>Second in the final is Shiba, 30.98 seconds.</b>

00:16:14.480 --> 00:16:18.580
<b>In 3rd grid, Hata, who showed excellent driving in the last minute of the qualifier.</b>

00:16:18.580 --> 00:16:20.760
<b>31.16 seconds!</b>

00:16:20.760 --> 00:16:24.260
<b>Fourth grid, Taira, 31.18 seconds!</b>

00:16:25.050 --> 00:16:28.250
<b>Fifth grid, Daiki, 31.31 seconds!</b>

00:16:28.250 --> 00:16:29.720
<b>It's a battle of five cars!</b>

00:16:29.720 --> 00:16:33.210
<b>Moreover the last car is within the 31-second range!</b>

00:16:33.210 --> 00:16:37.110
<b>It's a high-level battle, rarely seen in FSRS!</b>

00:17:43.670 --> 00:17:45.710
<b>Start!</b>

00:17:45.710 --> 00:17:46.620
<i>All right.</i>

00:17:46.620 --> 00:17:47.680
<i>The start was good.</i>

00:17:48.550 --> 00:17:50.250
<b>All cars started nicely!</b>

00:17:50.250 --> 00:17:52.770
<b>They all head for the first corner as a group!</b>

00:17:59.940 --> 00:18:01.190
He's here!

00:18:03.070 --> 00:18:06.590
<b>Taira aggressively makes an attack at Hata from the inside, but she blocks!</b>

00:18:06.590 --> 00:18:07.770
<b>Great job, both of you!</b>

00:18:07.770 --> 00:18:09.030
<b>Nice battle!</b>

00:18:09.030 --> 00:18:11.330
Fifteen laps in this final race!

00:18:11.330 --> 00:18:13.990
Give it all you got!

00:18:15.080 --> 00:18:17.110
<i>He's really going for it.</i>

00:18:17.110 --> 00:18:19.540
<i>Although he was down, he's...</i>

00:18:19.540 --> 00:18:20.460
<i>He's...</i>

00:18:20.460 --> 00:18:22.170
He's Capeta!

00:18:22.170 --> 00:18:23.330
Go for it!

00:18:23.330 --> 00:18:25.960
Beat that stuck-up girl!

00:18:45.190 --> 00:18:49.600
<i>But students are nervous after a crash.</i>

00:18:49.600 --> 00:18:52.610
<i>They're scared of crashing again.</i>

00:18:52.610 --> 00:18:54.030
Capeta.

00:18:59.080 --> 00:19:02.210
<i>It's the fifth corner where you crashed, Taira.</i>

00:19:04.380 --> 00:19:05.710
<i>Get it back.</i>

00:19:05.710 --> 00:19:06.670
<i>Get it back!</i>

00:19:16.640 --> 00:19:17.780
<i>Okay.</i>

00:19:17.780 --> 00:19:19.820
<i>He's driving like before.</i>

00:19:19.820 --> 00:19:21.100
<i>Good.</i>

00:19:45.880 --> 00:19:47.450
Capeta... you...

00:19:47.450 --> 00:19:49.460
Go!  Go!

00:20:12.650 --> 00:20:14.840
Don't you think there's something wrong with him?

00:20:14.840 --> 00:20:15.860
What is?

00:20:15.860 --> 00:20:18.470
No, it's as if he's panicking.

00:20:18.470 --> 00:20:21.160
It's like he's not himself.

00:20:21.570 --> 00:20:22.430
I wonder why.

00:20:22.430 --> 00:20:23.480
What are you talking about?

00:20:23.480 --> 00:20:24.810
Of course!

00:20:24.810 --> 00:20:27.170
He has to make up for the loss.

00:20:33.590 --> 00:20:35.940
Aha!  I see!  Now I get it!

00:20:35.940 --> 00:20:37.010
His line is different!

00:20:37.010 --> 00:20:38.740
His line is different?

00:20:38.740 --> 00:20:41.750
Compared to the rest, his line is sharper...

00:20:41.750 --> 00:20:43.840
or rather he's entering the first corner too sharply!

00:20:43.840 --> 00:20:46.650
That's why he's turning harder than he should.

00:20:47.010 --> 00:20:49.130
What are you panicking for, Capeta?!

00:20:49.130 --> 00:20:52.520
Your emotions are heating up and your time is suffering!

00:20:52.520 --> 00:20:53.980
Shut up, Nobu!

00:20:53.980 --> 00:20:55.130
It's Ca-chan.

00:20:55.130 --> 00:20:56.660
He must have some plan!

00:20:56.660 --> 00:20:58.870
Stop saying negative stuff!

00:20:59.250 --> 00:21:01.330
<i>Capeta... you...</i>

00:21:08.950 --> 00:21:10.230
<i>It's no good.</i>

00:21:10.230 --> 00:21:11.760
<i>Just a bit more...</i>

00:21:11.760 --> 00:21:13.600
<i>I should be able to do more...</i>

00:21:15.120 --> 00:21:16.430
<i>More!</i>

00:22:50.870 --> 00:22:53.430
Don't you think there's something wrong with his driving?

00:22:53.430 --> 00:22:55.650
Calm down, Capeta!

00:22:55.650 --> 00:22:56.810
What are you talking about?

00:22:56.810 --> 00:22:59.180
What's the point if he doesn't win the final?!

00:22:59.180 --> 00:23:01.200
Ca-chan!  Go, go!

00:23:01.200 --> 00:23:02.030
Next time, on Capeta.

00:23:02.030 --> 00:23:03.280
Heat Up!

00:23:03.280 --> 00:23:05.120
Open up the future!
